If you are not yet intrinsicly poison resistant, that =oPR should not
leave your finger until you are.

I usually play wishless, so I will point out a few observations on
what you DONT need to wish for, based on your very substantial
inventory.

You don't need to wish for SDSM.  You have a cursed scroll which can
be blanked, a magic marker, Magicbane, and a ring of lev.  Assuming
you can maximize your luck, it is trivial to write a cursed scroll of
genocide and clobber a roomful of silver dragons.  Using Magicbane to
engrave Elbereth and levitation to avoid damaging your engravings,
there is no danger of getting hit, or of the dragons running away. 
You would bump your XP level up, and get cold resistance.  Make sure
you are not satiated before you try to eat any dragons, though.  And
do be careful.  A typo moving you off the Elbereth square instead of
hitting a dragon is probably an insta-death.

26 daggers is overkill.  If you make use of Elbereth, ten daggers is
plenty.

You can also write unknown spellbooks easily if you maximize your
luck. Identify, Magic missile, charm monster, jumping, and create
monster can all be extremely useful.  You are a mid-level wizard,
spells should be your primary defense/offense.

If you are not opposed to wishing for artifacts, the blessed Orb of
Fate is a powerful artifact well worth a wish. It acts as a luckstone,
it effectively doubles your hitpoints (via half damage), it provides
occasional levelports and constant warning, and lastly it acts as a
regular crystal ball.  It is quite heavy, though. The only other quest
artifact that might be worth wishing for would be The Staff of
Aesculapius, although if you have wishes to spare, the Eyes of the
Overworld and the PYEC are also useful.

A blessed bag of holding is not a bad wish.  Another choice would be a
ring of polymorph control or another magic marker.

